    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Upload images in Block Editor directly to Imgur. You need <a href=\"https://api.imgur.com/oauth2/addclient\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">API credentials</a> from Imgur to use this plugin.</p>\n<h3>Hints</h3>\n<p>This plugin is not part of Imgur&#8217;s services. It was developed independently to make the good service of Imgur usable in WordPress. Questions about Imgur itself should be directed to their support: <a href=\"https://help.imgur.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">https://help.imgur.com</a></p>\n<p>The Imgur logo as part of all distributed icons is a trademark of <a href=\"https://imgur.com/tos\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">MediaLab.Ai Inc.</a>.</p>\n<h3>Repository</h3>\n<p>The development repository is on <a href=\"https://github.com/threadi/image-upload-for-imgur\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">GitHub</a>.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload &#8220;image-upload-for-imgur&#8221; to the &#8220;/wp-content/plugins/&#8221; directory.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8220;Plugins&#8221; menu in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Enter your imgur API credentials in the settings.</li>\n<li>Use the Block &#8220;Image Upload via Imgur&#8221;.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"can%20i%20use%20the%20plugin%20without%20an%20imgur%20account%3F\">\nCan I use the plugin without an Imgur account?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>The plugin can be installed even without Imgur account. However, it is not usable without Imgur API credentials.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.6</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Optimized block components for future versions of WordPress</li>\n<li>Set compatibility with WordPress 7.0</li>\n<li>Optimized compatibility with actual WordPress Coding Standards</li>\n<li>Updated dependencies</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/threadi/image-upload-for-imgur/blob/master/changelog.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">older changes</a></p>\n"
    },
